one of the industries which has just  exploded in growth this year  is telehealth according to the medical  economics 2020 health  ehr survey more than 77 percent of  doctors surveyed  used telehealth for the very first time  because of covet 19. so  gone are the days when you need to make  an appointment and wait weeks to get  into a doctor's office  in today's health watch online provider  nurex says this type of care  is here to stay copit has really shined  a light on how you can get personalized  quality care with telehealth nurex  serves 300  000 patients a month and is growing  instead of being a second or third  choice for care  nurex ceo varsha rao believes it's now  the first  choice for many women so all you do is  you fill out a medical history online  just like you would when you arrive at a  doctor's office  but then you chat or private message  with a provider  patients always have the opportunity to  ask questions  and to have interactions and many times  our patients are telling us that our  providers are giving them more  information better  information more education than what  they're getting in in-person settings  now some health insurance companies do  include telehealth as a benefit  in fact a study done this summer shows  physicians are still concerned about the  security of it  the workflow integration and also being  reimbursed for telehealth  even though 76 percent of people are  interested in it just 46 percent of  people surveyed  actually used it but that could change  as we continue to move through this  world in a post-pandemic world
 

